{
 "title": "The Object Info node",
 "summary": "One material, different colours per object. Five UV spheres duplicated (Shift+D) share a red material; an Object Info node's Random output into a colour ramp with five constant stops (blue, green, red, yellow, pink at 0, 0.25, 0.5, 0.75, 1) gives each a random colour (repeats possible) while metallic and roughness stay shared. A second row uses the Object Index output: each sphere's Pass Index set 1..5 (Object Properties > Relations) and divided by 5 in a Math node so the ramp gets 0.2..1 -- one colour each. Beyond the tutorial: the Location output colours nine blocks by where they stand, with Random varying their brightness.",
